true
`git_push`: the branch lane has no upstream; `git_push(repo, {branch = "lane"})` pushes it to origin's lane and makes that its upstream
origin/lane
refs/heads/lane on the lane
refs/heads/master first

`git_push`: the branch hand tracks origin's master, another name, and a bare push goes only to its own; `git_push(repo, {branch = "hand"})` pushes it to origin's hand and makes that its upstream
`git_push`: HEAD is detached, on no branch; `git_push(repo, {branch = "<name>"})` names one
refs/heads/lane on the lane
refs/heads/master first

`git_worktree_add` takes a `branch` or a `rev`, not both, unless the branch is `new`: then `rev` is where it starts
